From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:41:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: add the sg-pc system menu, save/load screens and message
 box, enable saving

Profile data plus two small generic extensions of the MO6TW/MO6TWPC UI classes; no S;G-specific C++.

STEINS;GATE (Steam) speaks the same script protocol as the classes the memo06 PC profile already uses, so the
profile only has to point at the right art:
  - System menu (SystemMenuType.MO6TW): SW_SYSMENUALPHA/SW_SYSMENUCNO are the numbers the S;G scripts use (2143, 3338),
    the twelve entries are the order of the script's JumpTable (BACK LOG, QUICK SAVE, QUICK LOAD, SAVE, LOAD, TIPS LIST,
    CONFIG, FULL SCREEN, HELP, RETURN TITLE, CLOSE MENU, EXIT GAME). The sprites are measured on DATA01.DDS (grey icon,
    white icon and italic label per row, the rounded panel behind the icons).
  - Saving: SaveDataType.MO6TWPC. The S;G scripts use the Chaos;Child style Save/AutoSave protocol and the CC ScrWork/
    flag layout that implementation persists; own file format. The SGHD special case in LoadSystemData (OK without a
    save system) is no longer reached.
  - Save, Load and Quick Load screens (SaveMenuType.MO6TWPC) over SAVEMENU/LOADMENU/QLOADMENU (system.mpk 26/12/25).
  - System message box (SysMesBoxType.MO6TW): "Load this Data?" with OK / Cancel. SYSMESSWINDOW/GSYSMES are fully
    transparent 128x128 sheets (the game draws its box procedurally), so the box pieces are cut from a dark part of
    the Data sheet.
  - charset.lua gets the ASCII -> glyph id map the engine needs for text it lays out itself (slot numbers, dates).

Generic extensions (backward compatible, memo06 PC unchanged):
  - MO6TW SystemMenu: when the profile lists one focused sprite per entry (MenuEntriesHighlightedSprites, which the
    loader already read for other menu types) it is drawn for the focused entry and the hover area covers both
    sprites; with MenuEntriesHNum 0 nothing changes.
  - MO6TWPC SaveMenu: optional per-mode background sprites (SaveBackgroundSprite, LoadBackgroundSprite,
    QuickLoadBackgroundSprite) for games whose three screens are separate pictures; they fall back to
    SaveMenuBackgroundSprite.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15) with original English data: the menu key opens the system menu with the twelve icons, the
focused row shows its label, BACK LOG opens the backlog and CLOSE MENU closes the menu; Save shows six slots with
thumbnails, play time and date after saving slot 1; Load shows the confirmation box and restores the saved line.
Not done: the slot highlight and PREV/NEXT art (the sheets have none; PREV/NEXT are invisible tap areas), CONFIG,
TIPS, HELP, RETURN TITLE and EXIT GAME screens, and leaving the save screen with Back (in the test the script kept polling the 00:53 instruction, which the engine
stubs as ClickOnJump).

