+-- STEINS;GATE (Steam) save / load / quick load screens, drawn by the generic SaveMenuType.MO6TWPC class (six entries per
+-- page, PREV/NEXT, thumbnail, number, play time and date text) over the three pictures SAVEMENU (system.mpk id 26),
+-- LOADMENU (12) and QLOADMENU (25). Each is a 3072x1080 sheet: the screen at (0, 0, 1920x1080) with its title baked in
+-- (a big dark panel at x 85..1840, y 108..978), and at x >= 1920 a banner (1920,0, 791x165), the "NO DATA" thumbnail
+-- (2713,1, 241x136), the page digits (y 175..226, "/6" after them), three coloured bars and two lock icons (y 283).
+-- The sheet has no card, highlight or button art, so those use a transparent patch (x >= 1950, y >= 500 is empty) and
+-- the engine draws the numbers, times and dates as text; the thumbnails are 240x135 like the NO DATA one.
+-- NOT measurable from the sheet: where the native game puts the entries. Two columns of three rows inside the panel,
+-- PREV / NEXT as invisible 280x60 tap areas at the bottom of the panel with the page text between them, are estimates.
